# Copy to .env.local for local development. .env.local is gitignored and must
# stay that way — the real values live only in Vercel's Environment Variables.
#
# NEVER prefix any of these with NEXT_PUBLIC_. That prefix inlines the value
# into the JavaScript that ships to the browser.

# ── Anthropic ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used only by /api/generate, and only after a payment has been verified.
# If unset, a paid customer still gets the deterministic fallback routine
# rather than an error.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ── Stripe ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRET. Stripe -> Developers -> API keys.
#
# The key decides the environment: a _test_ key takes test cards only, a _live_
# one charges real cards. There is no separate "go live" flag to forget —
# swapping this key IS going live. Use a test key until you have bought a
# routine yourself and watched it arrive.
#
# Either a full secret key (sk_) or a restricted key (rk_) works. A restricted
# key only has the permissions ticked when it was created, and RŌZU needs:
#     Checkout Sessions   WRITE   (creating a checkout is a write, not a read)
#     Prices              READ    (only so /api/setup can check them for you)
# A missing permission is invisible until a customer presses Unlock, so run
# /api/setup once after setting this — it makes the same calls.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# SECRET. Stripe -> Developers -> Webhooks -> add an endpoint pointing at
# https://<your site>/api/webhook, then copy its signing secret (whsec_...).
# Subscribe it to exactly these events:
#     checkout.session.completed
#     checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded
#     charge.refunded
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Not secret. PRICE ids, not product ids — a price starts with price_, a
# product with prod_. One product can have several prices, so a prod_ id does
# not say what to charge and the checkout will refuse it. Open each product in
# the Stripe dashboard and copy the id from its pricing section.
STRIPE_PRICE_SOLO=
STRIPE_PRICE_COUPLE=
STRIPE_PRICE_GIFT=

# ── Tax ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stripe Tax is ON unless this is explicitly 0/false/no/off.
#
# Read this once: Stripe is NOT a merchant of record. Lemon Squeezy was, and it
# collected and remitted tax on your behalf. Stripe does not. You are the
# seller, and registering and filing is yours to do — Stripe Tax only works out
# what to charge, and only in jurisdictions where you have added a registration
# under Stripe -> Tax. With none added it calculates zero and checkout still
# works, which is the safe way for this to be wrong.
#
# Each price must also have a tax_behavior set (inclusive or exclusive) or
# Stripe refuses the checkout outright. Inclusive keeps $9 as the total the
# customer pays. /api/setup checks this and says so.
# STRIPE_TAX=0

# ── Proof-of-payment token ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRET. Any random string, 32+ characters. Signs the token that /api/generate
# accepts as proof an order was paid for. Rotating it invalidates every token
# already issued, so a customer mid-purchase would lose access.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
ROZU_TOKEN_SECRET=

# ── Storage ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pick ONE. Supabase wins if both are set.
#
# Supabase. SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is SECRET — it bypasses row level
# security. Never the anon key, and never NEXT_PUBLIC_. Needs the rozu_kv table;
# /api/setup prints the SQL.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
#
# Or Upstash Redis, set automatically by Vercel -> Storage. Do not type these by
# hand in production.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
#
# With neither, the app falls back to an in-process map so `next dev` works
# without a database. That fallback refuses to serve checkout in production,
# because an order it forgets is an order that was paid for and never
# delivered.

# ── Redemption codes (Etsy and any other off-Stripe channel) ─────────────────
# SECRET, 16+ characters. Gates code minting at
#     /api/setup?mint=<this>&plan=solo&count=10
# ROZU_SETUP must ALSO be on for that to work. Two separate gates on purpose:
# the setup page is readable by anyone while ROZU_SETUP is set, and minting
# free routines behind that alone would be an open tap.
#
# Unlike the preview key, this one is safe to keep: knowing it mints codes,
# which is worth nothing without also being the person handing them to buyers.
# Codes themselves are single-use and carry their own plan, so a code cannot be
# spent twice or upgraded to a bigger plan than it was sold as.
# ROZU_ADMIN_KEY=

# ── Preview mode (temporary, for reviewing the finished result) ──────────────
# SECRET, 16+ characters. While set, visiting /?preview=<value> makes the
# Unlock button skip Stripe: the order is written already marked paid and
# everything after that — token, AI call, caching — runs exactly as it does for
# a real customer. Anyone who knows the value gets free routines, so DELETE THIS
# BEFORE LAUNCH. /api/setup shouts about it while it is set.
# ROZU_PREVIEW_KEY=

# ── Attribution (public by design) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Pixel IDs appear in the page source of every site that uses them, so
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is correct here — and only here. Nothing loads until the visitor
# accepts the consent banner. Leave unset and no pixel exists at all.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TIKTOK_PIXEL_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LINKEDIN_PARTNER_ID=

# ── Site ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. The canonical origin used to build the post-payment return URL.
# Derived from the request when unset, which is correct on Vercel. Set it once
# there is a custom domain.
# ROZU_SITE_URL=https://rozu.example
